urnal">Mokranjac, D., and W. Neupert. <year>2005</year>. Protein import into mitochondria. <source>Biochem. Soc. Trans.</source> <volume>33</volume>:<fpage>1019</fpage>&#x02013;1023.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16246036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal">Nao&#x000e9;, M., Y. Ohwa, D. Ishikawa, C. Ohshima, S. Nishikawa, H. Yamamoto, and T. Endo. <year>2004</year>. Identification of Tim40 that mediates protein sorting to the mitochondrial intermembrane space. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>279</volume>:<fpage>47815</fpage>&#x02013;47821.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15364952</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal">Rehling, P., N. Pfanner, and C. Meisinger. <year>2003</year>. Insertion of hydrophobic membrane proteins into the inner mitochondrial membrane&#x02014;a guided tour. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>326</volume>:<fpage>639</fpage>&#x02013;657.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12581629</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Rehling, P., K. Brander, and N. Pfanner. <year>2004</year>. Mitochondrial import and the twin-pore translocase. <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>5</volume>:<fpage>519</fpage>&#x02013;530.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15232570</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Sch&#x000e4;gger, H. <year>2001</year>. Blue-native gels to isolate protein complexes from mitochondria. <source>Methods Cell Biol.</source> <volume>65</volume>:<fpage>231</fpage>&#x02013;244.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11381596</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Wiedemann, N., A.E. Frazier, and N. Pfanner. <year>2004</year>. The protein import machinery of mitochondria. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>279</volume>:<fpage>14473</fpage>&#x02013;14476.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14973134</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Yamamoto, H., T. Momose, Y. Yatsukawa, C. Ohshima, D. Ishikawa, T. Sato, Y. Tamura, Y. Ohwa, and T. Endo. <year>2005</year>. Identification of a novel member of yeast mitochondrial Hsp70-associated motor and chaperone proteins that facilitates protein translocation across the inner membrane. <source>FEBS Lett.</source> <volume>579</volume>:<fpage>507</fpage>&#x02013;511.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15642367</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>